For each thread, decide on one verdict:
- addressed: the concern is fixed, or correctly answered.
- not_addressed: still a problem; say what's missing.
- unclear: needs @$me's judgement (design disagreement, product call); say why.

Point out any claim in the author's replies that the code contradicts, even when the thread is addressed.

Then look at the new commits for problems that none of the threads covers. Report only ones you're certain of, and don't repeat existing comments, CodeRabbit's included.

Format code references as markdown links to the absolute path in the worktree with a line anchor, e.g. [path:42]($worktree/path#L42).

